> days(m: u8 in 1..12) = match m { 2 => 28, 4 | 6 | 9 | 11 => 30, _ => 31 }
> find days
  note: the result is int: searching in u8
find days: 12 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030
  rewrites the model prices lower (each derived, with what it holds under):
  cost 6   int(0x3bbeecc >> (u32(m) << 1) & 3) + 28 the map m == 2 ? 28 : m == 4 || m == 6 || m == 9 || m == 11 ? 30 : 3… (1 more characters) of m as a table in one constant (12 entries of 2 bits) (derived; checked on every point)
      holds where m in [1, 12] (its range)
      m == 2 ? 28 : m == 4 || m == 6 || m == 9 || m == 11 ? 30 : 3… (1 more characters) at m = 1..12 is [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31] (evaluated at each of the 12)
      bits [2*i, 2*i + 2) of 0x3bbeecc hold the value at m = i, less the least value: shifting right by that many bits times m and masking reads it
  cost 6   u8(0x3bbeecc >> (u32(m) << 1) & 3) + 28  packed table in one constant
  cost 8   [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31][m - 1] lookup table (baseline)
  [searched every term up to cost 5: 1398101 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]
> range days
range of days -> int:
  28..31
  fits in u5
  over all 12 points of the domain
